 {r}←RemoveSupersededPackages folder;F;ns;listed;names;types;dirs;keep;i;rc;msg;ids;noticeFile;lines;encoding;nl;heads;sectionIDs;keepSection;sectionNo
⍝ Removes from `folder` every package that was fetched but not selected, and returns what went.\\
⍝ Tatin resolves dependencies by minimal version selection: a version named in a dependency file is
⍝ a *minimum*, and within a major version line the highest of those minimums is the one selected.
⍝ The ones that lost stay behind in the install folder, while `apl-buildlist.json` names the selected
⍝ ones only - so the build list, not the folder listing, says what the code actually loads.\\
⍝ For an install folder that is correct and there is nothing to do. A distribution is a different
⍝ matter: it should carry what is loaded and nothing besides, which is why this runs before the ZIP
⍝ is built.\\
⍝ `NOTICE.md` is pruned to match, because it carries a licence section per package *fetched*, and a
⍝ notice naming software that is not in the ZIP is no more correct than one that omits software
⍝ that is.\\
⍝ Nothing happens when there is no build list, because then there is nothing to go by.
 F←##.Cider.FilesAndDirs
 r←⍬
 :If ⎕NEXISTS folder,'/apl-buildlist.json'
     ns←⎕JSON⍠('Dialect' 'JSON5')⊢⊃⎕NGET folder,'/apl-buildlist.json'
     listed←'/'∘,¨,⊆ns.packageID                            ⍝ Anchored on the separator because one group name may end with another
     (names types)←0 1 ⎕NINFO⍠('Wildcard' 1)⊢folder,'/*'
     dirs←{'/'@('\'∘=)⊢⍵↓⍨-(¯1↑⍵)∊'/\'}¨(types=1)/names     ⍝ 1 is a directory, 2 a regular file
     keep←(⊂listed){∨/⍺{⍺≡(-≢⍺)↑⍵}¨⊂⍵}¨dirs
     :For i :In ⍸~keep
         (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce i⊃dirs
         msg Assert rc=0
     :EndFor
     r←(~keep)/dirs
     ids←{⊃¯1↑(⍵≠'/')⊆⍵}¨r
     noticeFile←folder,'/NOTICE.md'
     :If 0<≢ids
     :AndIf ⎕NEXISTS noticeFile
⍝ The licence sections are a flat list of "## <packageID>" blocks, so a section runs up to the next
⍝ such line. Anything before the first one is a preamble and is kept whatever happens.
         (lines encoding nl)←⎕NGET noticeFile 1
         heads←(⊂'## ')≡¨3↑¨lines
         sectionIDs←3↓¨heads/lines
         keepSection←~sectionIDs∊ids
         sectionNo←+\heads
         lines←((1,keepSection)[1+sectionNo])/lines
         (lines encoding nl)⎕NPUT noticeFile 1
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
